  "hindi": "अग्नि ने, प्रसन्न मन वाले होकर, चमकती हुई उषाओं के अग्रभाग की ओर, रत्नों के दान की ओर देखा है। हे अश्विनौ, सुकर्मी के घर आओ; सूर्य देव प्रकाश के साथ ऊपर उठता है।",
  "english": "Agni, kindly-minded, has looked towards the foremost part of the shining dawns, towards the bestowal of treasure. Come, Aśvins, to the house of the well-doer; the god Sūrya goes up with light.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "pratyagniḥ = prati agniḥ (prati the preverb of akhyat), not pratyaṅ. akhyat 'has looked towards' (prati-√khyā) is the most literal sense; 'has shone upon' is an alternative. sukṛtaḥ taken as gen. sg. 'of the well-doer'; acc. pl. is also possible. ut eti 'goes up'.",
  "confidence": "medium"
 },
