  "hindi": "देव सविता ने ऊपर की ओर तेज को उठाया है, बूँद को हिलाते हुए, गौओं की खोज करने वाले योद्धा के समान। जब वे सूर्य को आकाश में चढ़ाते हैं, तब वरुण और मित्र व्रत के अनुसार चलते हैं।",
  "english": "The god Savitṛ has raised the radiance upward, shaking the drop, like a warrior seeking cattle. Varuṇa and Mitra go along the ordinance when they make the Sun mount in the sky.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "gaviṣaḥ: form uncertain; taken as 'seeking cattle' with satvā 'warrior' (Padapāṭha gaviṣaḥ; gen. sg. of gaviṣ 'quest for cattle' is the other possibility, 'like a warrior of the quest for cattle'). yanti is plural though only Varuṇa and Mitra are named; further subjects may be implied (the plural ārohayanti too). anu ... yanti 'go along/follow'. Source marks ṷ in anṷ, varṷṇo are notation.",
  "confidence": "medium"
 },
