  "hindi": "जिसे उन्होंने अन्धकार के लिए, वियोग के लिए बनाया, दृढ़ आश्रय वाले, बिना रुके, प्रयोजन के लिए — उस सूर्य को, समस्त जगत् के द्रष्टा को, सात भूरे-पीले, बलवान् ढोते हैं।",
  "english": "Whom they made for the darkness, for separation, those of firm abode, not resting, for the purpose — that Sūrya, the watcher of the whole moving world, the seven tawny, vigorous ones carry.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "Obscure first half. vipṛce (dat. of vipṛc 'separation / to separate'), anavasyantaḥ (pres. part., 'not resting' is a guess) and artham are uncertain; translated literally without supplying a sense. The subject of akṛṇvan is not stated. haritaḥ/yahvīḥ taken as the seven tawny ones (mares) carrying Sūrya.",
